afk: yield accepts whole-array payloads for array-valued sections.

The yield tool's parameter schema (withSectionVariants) advertises the
whole array branch for array-valued sections like `findings`, but the
per-section validator only accepted a single element and assembly nested
a submitted array one level deep — every reviewer that batched findings
burned schema-retry round trips. Array payloads for array-valued
sections now validate against the property schema and splat into the
section; the tool description says so.

What must survive a rebase:
- output-schema-validator.ts: the per-section validator (and the
  per-section strict-null normalizer) for an array-typed property
  accepts the full array (checked against the property schema) as well
  as one element (items schema).
- The section assembler splats an array payload for array-valued labels
  instead of nesting it. Since 18.2.x that assembler lives in
  packages/tui/src/tools/task-yield-assembly.ts (appendYieldSection,
  shape "array"); coding-agent's task/yield-assembly.ts only computes
  the label shapes (yieldSectionShapes since 18.6.0).
- Regression test in test/tools/yield.test.ts (whole-array accept,
  invalid element still rejected per call, splat + append on assembly).

Rebased 18.2.10 -> 18.6.0: upstream still validates array sections
per element and still nests array payloads, so the patch stays.
Upstream split section-schema derivation into buildSectionSchemas (now
also feeding the new strict-null normalizeSection) and replaced the
assembler's boolean `forceArray`/arrayValuedLabels with
YieldSectionShapes ("array" | "scalar") / yieldSectionShapes(). Re-cut:
buildSectionSchemas keeps both the items schema and the whole property
schema for array properties, and one selector (sectionSchemaFor) picks
the property schema for array payloads in BOTH the section validator and
normalizeSection, so whole-array payloads also get strict-null
normalization. appendYieldSection splats array payloads when the shape is
"array". The regression test uses yieldSectionShapes.

